  "id": "COMPOUND:980 - PROTEIN:5230",
  "verbalization": "Doxorubicin is implicated in the relationship with LB2241-RCC through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that doxorubicin targets P2X purinoceptor 1, which is subsequently targeted by [(1R)-1-[(5Z)-4-Bromo-5-(Bromomethylidene)-2-Oxofuran-3-Yl]Butyl] Acetate, a compound that also binds to GDM-1 and ultimately affects LB2241-RCC. This pathway indicates a potential mechanism where doxorubicin indirectly influences LB2241-RCC through the activation of P2X purinoceptors, possibly via the action of the aforementioned compound. The shared target of [(1R)-1-[(5Z)-4-Bromo-5-(Bromomethylidene)-2-Oxofuran-3-Yl]Butyl] Acetate and LB2241-RCC suggests a possible role in cellular signaling or metabolic pathways that are dysregulated in the disease. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between doxorubicin and LB2241-RCC, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
